# Semantic HTML — article, div, a

Use `<article>` **only** for blog-related content: post cards, single post body, blog archive items, and other standalone blog entries.

Everywhere else, use `<div>`. If the block is clickable or navigates somewhere, wrap it in `<a>` instead of `<div>`.

## Do

```html
<!-- Blog post card -->
<article class="blog-card">...</article>

<!-- Single post content -->
<article class="single-post-content">...</article>

<!-- Non-blog card (no link) -->
<div class="flex flex-col rounded-[20px] border ...">...</div>

<!-- Clickable card -->
<a href="<?php echo esc_url($url); ?>" class="flex flex-col rounded-[20px] border ... no-underline">...</a>
```

## Don't

```html
<!-- ❌ article for non-blog UI (steps, features, team, etc.) -->
<article class="structure-session-step">...</article>

<!-- ❌ div when the whole block is a link -->
<div onclick="location.href='...'">...</div>
```

## Quick check

- Blog post or blog listing item → `<article>`
- Static UI block, step, feature, team member, certificate → `<div>`
- Entire block is a link → `<a>`
